  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two bodies collide on a horizontal frictionless surface. Body X, of mass 2.0 kg, moves with an initial speed of 0.80 m s<sub>−1</sub> and body Y is initially stationary. After the collision, body X moves at an angle of 90° to the initial direction of motion with a speed of 0.60 m s<sub>−1</sub>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>What is the magnitude of the momentum of body Y after the collision?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">0.40 kg m s<sub>−1</sub></li><li data-label=\"B\">1.0 kg m s<sub>−1</sub></li><li data-label=\"C\">2.0 kg m s<sub>−1</sub></li><li data-label=\"D\">2.8 kg m s<sub>−1</sub></li></ol>"
  },
